The v3 build is finished, passes every test I ran, and is packaged at `~/workspace/archive-rebuild/archive-rebuild-v3.zip` (1.8 MB). Nothing has gone to the owner.

**What I built.** An earlier session had already written the v3 app itself: the opening animation, the five-item nav with the About hub, the six-step path, the 40 days, the first lessons per level, tap-a-line transcripts, motion and themes. I picked it up from there and added:
- **`v3/build.py`** (standard library only). It produces two versions of the page:
  - `archive.html`: a single file with the catalog inside. This is what the launchers open.
  - `archive-hosted.html`: loads the catalog from a separate, versioned `catalog.js`, for hosting later.
  
  The build stops on any catalog drift, em dash, external URL, unfinished wording, or launcher/server change. I proved those checks work by feeding it an "awaiting" line, an em dash and a Google Fonts URL; each one stopped the build.
- **`docs/server-contract.md`**, plus HTTP, behavior and screenshot test scripts in `v3/tools/`.
- **Four layout fixes found in screenshot review:**
  - The lesson page was 485px wide on a 390px phone.
  - The big letter on the topic cards ran into the title.
  - The header shifted 1 to 2px when switching language.
  - Transcript times touched the text.

**Test results** (this VM, headless Chromium, final build):
- **Build:** the catalog is byte-identical to v2 (3,977 media entries, 71 playlists), and the server and both launchers are byte-identical to v2.
- **HTTP: 23/23 pass.** That's v2's 16, plus `catalog.js` serving, `/__status` with the recitation flag, and the hosted page.
- **Behavior: 14/14 pass:**
  - The header stays put on language switch.
  - The opening has one button, and clicking Enter mid-animation enters the library.
  - Reduced motion shows a still, complete frame.
  - Theme swatches switch live.
  - Tapping transcript line 2 jumps the video to 0:05.
  - A missing video shows the plain message with Details folded away.
  - Favorites saved by v2 still show.
  - Sort remembers its choice.
  - With the browser offline the page still works, with zero outside requests.
- **Screenshots: 65/65 pass** the automatic checks (desktop and mobile, Arabic and English, all six themes, errors). I looked through the main screens myself. My first overflow check missed the mobile bug, so I fixed the check too.

**Not verified:**
- Real MKV playback from the 1.02 TB library on the laptop. Only three tiny test files were played.
- The Windows and macOS launchers were not run.
- Safari and Firefox were not tested; only Chromium was.
- The hosted version was checked over HTTP but not seen in a browser on a real host.
- I read the brief in full but did not reread all four research reports; their design choices are as the earlier session built them.
- A native Arabic reader should check the wording.

